1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,432
Menus, breadcrumb trails and pagers are shapes in Orchard Core, so your theme

2
00:00:05,432 --> 00:00:06,927
decides how they look.

3
00:00:06,927 --> 00:00:10,505
This video shows how to render each one from a theme, and how

4
00:00:10,505 --> 00:00:12,160
to override its template.

5
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:20,626
A shape is a named piece of output that a template draws.

6
00:00:20,626 --> 00:00:26,395
To change the markup, add a template with the shape's name to your theme's Views folder.

7
00:00:26,395 --> 00:00:31,980
A more specific name, called an alternate, targets one menu, one trail, or one pager.

8
00:00:32,730 --> 00:00:38,020
The Menu module provides the Menu shape, for menus that editors build in the admin.

9
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:44,320
The Navigation module, which is always enabled, provides the Breadcrumb, Pager and PagerSlim shapes.

10
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:52,736
In a Razor layout, the menu tag helper renders a menu by its alias.

11
00:00:52,736 --> 00:00:57,645
The cache attributes, which need the Dynamic Cache feature, keep the output for

12
00:00:57,645 --> 00:01:00,590
five minutes and vary it by the user's roles.

13
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:06,762
Publishing the menu drops the cached copy, because the cache tag is the menu's alias.

14
00:01:06,762 --> 00:01:12,720
In Liquid, the shape tag takes the same values, with underscores in the cache parameter names.

15
00:01:14,337 --> 00:01:17,081
Let's edit Main Menu, in Content, Menus.

16
00:01:17,081 --> 00:01:21,674
Its Alias field holds main-menu, the name that the layout looks up with

17
00:01:21,674 --> 00:01:26,507
the alias prefix, and the two link items below it are what the theme draws.

18
00:01:26,963 --> 00:01:31,113
On the site, the layout renders that alias in the navigation bar.

19
00:01:31,113 --> 00:01:36,783
The links are the same items; only the markup around them comes from the theme's templates.

20
00:01:40,983 --> 00:01:45,921
The Menu template receives the menu shape and creates the outer list.

21
00:01:45,921 --> 00:01:51,253
It displays each entry of Model.Items, and every entry is a MenuItem shape.

22
00:01:52,003 --> 00:01:56,089
The MenuItem template draws one list item and its sub items.

23
00:01:56,089 --> 00:02:01,103
It displays the same shape again as a MenuItemLink, which draws the anchor.

24
00:02:01,853 --> 00:02:06,486
MenuItemLink has a template for each type of menu item, such as the

25
00:02:06,486 --> 00:02:09,024
link, content and HTML menu items.

26
00:02:09,024 --> 00:02:13,530
The address of a link or HTML item is checked before the template

27
00:02:13,530 --> 00:02:16,513
runs, so an unsafe address arrives empty.

28
00:02:17,263 --> 00:02:20,366
To target one case, use an alternate name.

29
00:02:20,366 --> 00:02:25,019
A menu's name is its title as one word, without spaces or hyphens,

30
00:02:25,019 --> 00:02:28,445
each word capitalized, as the first card shows.

31
00:02:28,445 --> 00:02:34,133
The name, a content type and a level combine, and the most specific template wins.

32
00:02:38,333 --> 00:02:42,221
Reference the Navigation Core tag helpers in your view imports.

33
00:02:42,221 --> 00:02:46,108
Then add the breadcrumb tag helper to a view, in the Title zone

34
00:02:46,108 --> 00:02:51,123
that the admin theme renders, with a stable name and the title of the current page.

35
00:02:51,873 --> 00:02:55,729
Declare only the ancestors as breadcrumb item children.

36
00:02:55,729 --> 00:02:59,901
Each links to an action or a URL, and a permission turns its

37
00:02:59,901 --> 00:03:02,999
link into plain text for users who lack it.

38
00:03:02,999 --> 00:03:06,223
The current page comes last, never as a link.

39
00:03:07,823 --> 00:03:15,147
To change the ancestors of any trail, implement IBreadcrumbProvider and register it with AddBreadcrumbProvider.

40
00:03:15,147 --> 00:03:19,967
A provider sees every visible trail, so it checks the trail name first.

41
00:03:19,967 --> 00:03:23,473
Providers run before the current page is appended.

42
00:03:25,074 --> 00:03:27,955
In the admin, edit an item of Main Menu.

43
00:03:27,955 --> 00:03:33,340
The trail reads Dashboard, Manage Content, Edit Main Menu, and the current page,

44
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:34,968
Edit Link Menu Item.

45
00:03:34,968 --> 00:03:40,604
The Dashboard link comes from a provider that the Admin Dashboard feature registers.

46
00:03:41,064 --> 00:03:46,719
The Show breadcrumb setting, under Settings, Admin, controls the trail on admin screens.

47
00:03:46,719 --> 00:03:48,524
Let's clear it and save.

48
00:03:48,987 --> 00:03:53,425
With it cleared, the same screen shows only the heading, because the tag

49
00:03:53,425 --> 00:03:55,587
helper always renders the title.

50
00:03:57,187 --> 00:04:01,346
The Breadcrumb template draws the trail and the heading together.

51
00:04:01,346 --> 00:04:06,033
The display type is DetailAdmin in the admin and Detail elsewhere, and the

52
00:04:06,033 --> 00:04:11,247
trail's name is another alternate, so a theme can restyle one trail or one context.

53
00:04:15,447 --> 00:04:20,766
In a controller, build a Pager from the request's PagerParameters and the PagerOptions,

54
00:04:20,766 --> 00:04:24,198
count the items, and create the shape with PagerAsync.

55
00:04:24,198 --> 00:04:28,717
Query only the items of the current page, and pass the shape to the view.

56
00:04:29,467 --> 00:04:35,651
The view displays the shape; in Liquid, the shape_pager tag sets its texts and classes first.

57
00:04:35,651 --> 00:04:40,023
The slim pager needs no item count, because it only links to the

58
00:04:40,023 --> 00:04:41,897
previous and next pages.

59
00:04:43,502 --> 00:04:47,323
On the home page of the blog, The Blog Theme draws the slim

60
00:04:47,323 --> 00:04:49,499
pager with the shape pager tag.

61
00:04:49,499 --> 00:04:54,202
The first page offers Older Posts, and the second page offers Newer Posts.

62
00:04:55,804 --> 00:05:00,626
In the admin, the list of Blog Post content items shows the full pager:

63
00:05:00,626 --> 00:05:05,448
numbered pages, with links to the first, previous, next and last pages.

64
00:05:05,448 --> 00:05:11,334
The Items per page selector at its end appears when the site allows page size selection.

65
00:05:12,934 --> 00:05:17,366
A theme restyles a pager by overriding the templates of its parts.

66
00:05:17,366 --> 00:05:21,798
The Default Theme wraps the pager in a nav element, and each part,

67
00:05:21,798 --> 00:05:27,214
such as Previous or Next, turns into a Pager_Link that adds the Bootstrap classes.

68
00:05:27,964 --> 00:05:32,818
When page size selection is allowed in Settings, General, both pagers render an

69
00:05:32,818 --> 00:05:34,531
Items per page selector.

70
00:05:34,531 --> 00:05:39,042
The Navigation module provides plain markup for it, and a theme styles it

71
00:05:39,042 --> 00:05:41,954
with its own Pager_PageSizeSelector template.

72
00:05:43,954 --> 00:05:47,730
That is how a theme renders menus, breadcrumb trails and pagers:

73
00:05:47,730 --> 00:05:52,152
shapes you call from a layout or a view, and templates you override by name.

74
00:05:52,152 --> 00:05:53,554
Thanks for watching.

